# Shell scripts run on Linux boxes, and a CRLF checkout breaks them at the
# shebang: `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` is not an interpreter any kernel knows, and
# the error ("no such file or directory" naming a binary that plainly exists)
# sends people hunting in the wrong place. This repo is edited on Windows and
# its scripts are copied to trades-box-1, so pin them.
*.sh text eol=lf
